@@ -106,6 +106,8 @@ At the first eligible `agent/pre-step` of a session, the plugin composes the bas
 
 Every injected message carries a typed source with its change list; a complete baseline also carries an identity derived from normalized discovery, precedence, project-root, and budget configuration, and a matching durable message confirms a queued baseline. Model-visible text contains no hidden state markers, and literal `</system-reminder>` text anywhere in instruction content or model-visible metadata is escaped so repository-controlled text cannot close the plugin-owned frame.
 
+`candidateSelection: first` chooses one confirmed non-empty project candidate per directory. Unavailable higher-priority candidates retain the prior winner through the native group rollback. `fileTouchToolNames` configures successful native or deployment file touches. `globalInstructionRoots` selects existing `dsh` and `agents` global roots; its default keeps both in native precedence, while a deployment may explicitly retain only its previously authorized root. Project selection never collapses the independent global roots.
+
 </details>
 
